            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="NAS01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>Andrew and George</forename>
                        <surname>Nash</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation>glass manufactureres</occupation>
                    <occupation>money brokers</occupation>
                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>The Nash brothers were used by Shelley 
    for his post obit bond in 1814.  The bond was for £8,000, for 
    which they paid £2,593-10s. Shelley's father attempted to buy 
    the bond back in February 1816, offering £4,500.  (See St Clair, p. 353-5, and p.385). Godwin and 
    Shelley see a good deal of them during Shelley and Godwin's 
    financial crises of 1814.</p>
                        <p>The later entries for Nash are to <persName key="NAS02">John Nash</persName>, 
  the architect, wth whom Godwin apprenticed William in 1820.</p>
                    </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">St Clair, <title>The Godwins and the Shelleys</title></bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
